WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Extending the Need for Performance Baselining

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.833
Hello, Mike Harry with you again, where we're going to explore the idea of baselines.

3
00:00:10.833 --> 00:00:15.699
And how to establish those baselines. And why they're so critical.

4
00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:20.033
to the operation of a business or a process.

5
00:00:20.033 --> 00:00:25.366
You know, in order to gauge a relative speed. And the key word there is relative.

6
00:00:25.366 --> 00:00:31.832
A relative speed, a relative performance, we need to benchmark that against some

7
00:00:31.833 --> 00:00:35.833
stake in the ground. And that's a baseline.

8
00:00:35.833 --> 00:00:42.199
Only then can we determine our rate of change, how fast we’re moving, etc.

9
00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:47.366
It’s kind of our lighthouse, if you will. It's what we look back to

10
00:00:47.366 --> 00:00:50.632
to determine our course, direction, and speed.

11
00:00:50.633 --> 00:00:56.666
We’re going to get into this and come to understand baselines very well,

12
00:00:56.666 --> 00:01:01.666
because it is so essential to the use of Six Sigma.

13
00:01:01.666 --> 00:01:06.666
Thank you for choosing SSMI.
